 I'm here to help you design an End User API (EUA) for 3D camera animation in TypeScript. The EUA should be easy to use, efficient, and flexible enough to accommodate various animation requirements. Here's a suggested design:

1. **Camera class:** Create a Camera class as the core component of your EUA. This class will have methods to set position, orientation, and zoom level.

```typescript
class Camera {
  private _position: Vector3;
  private _orientation: Quaternion;
  private _zoomLevel: number;

  constructor() {
    this._position = new Vector3(0, 0, 10); // Default position
    this._orientation = new Quaternion();
    this._zoomLevel = 45; // Default zoom level
  }

  setPosition(x: number, y: number, z: number): void {
    this._position.set(x, y, z);
  }

  setOrientation(q: Quaternion): void {
    this._orientation.copy(q);
  }

  setZoomLevel(level: number): void {
    this._zoomLevel = level;
  }

  get position(): Vector3 {
    return this._position;
  }

  get orientation(): Quaternion {
    return this._orientation;
  }

  get zoomLevel(): number {
    return this._zoomLevel;
  }
}
```

2. **Animation classes:** Create separate animation classes for different types of camera movements like Translation, Rotation, Zoom, etc. These classes should inherit from an abstract AnimationBase class.

```typescript
abstract class AnimationBase {
  protected _duration: number;
  protected _easingFunction: EasingFunction;
  protected _camera: Camera;

  constructor(camera: Camera, duration: number, easingFunction?: EasingFunction) {
    this._camera = camera;
    this._duration = duration;
    this._easingFunction = easingFunction || new LinearEasingFunction(); // Default is Linear
  }

  abstract update(deltaTime: number): void;
}

