 To apply a Gaussian filter before the Sobel edge detection algorithm in MATLAB, you need to add an extra step to your existing code. Here's how you can modify your code to apply a Gaussian filter followed by the Sobel edge detection:
```matlab
% Read input image and convert to grayscale
input_image = imread('image.jpg');
gray_image = rgb2gray(input_image);
% Apply Gaussian filter
gaussian_filter_size = [3 3]; % Define the size of the Gaussian filter kernel (odd numbers)
sigma = 0.5; % Define the standard deviation of the Gaussian filter
gaussian_filter = fspecial('gaussian', gaussian_filter_size, sigma);
filtered_image = imfilter(gray_image, gaussian_filter);
% Define Sobel operators in x and y directions
sobel_x = [-1 0 1; -2 0 2; -1 0 1];
sobel_y = [-1 -2 -1; 0 0 0; 1 2 1];
% Apply Sobel operator in x direction
edge_image_x = conv2(double(filtered_image), sobel_x, 'same');
% Apply Sobel operator in y direction
edge_image_y = conv2(double(filtered_image), sobel_y, 'same');
% Combine edges in both directions
edge_image = sqrt(edge_image_x.^2 + edge_image_y.^2);
% Display original image, filtered image, and edge image
subplot(1,3,1), imshow(input_image), title('Original Image');
subplot(1,3,2), imshow(filtered_image), title('Filtered Image');
subplot(1,3,3), imshow(edge_image), title('Edge Image');
```
In this modified code, we first read the input image and convert it to grayscale as before. Then, we define the size and standard deviation of the Gaussian filter kernel and create the Gaussian filter using the `fspecial` function. We apply the Gaussian filter to the grayscale image using the `imfilter` function.

